        "original_id": "b73702ce-aa5d-536d-909d-7993ccbe2de7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Symbolic Manipulation Program (SMP), A New Kind of Science\n- People: Chris A. Cole, Stephen Wolfram, Geoffrey C. Fox, Jeffrey M. Greif, Eric D. Mjolsness, Larry J. Romans, Timothy Shaw, Anthony E. Terrano\n- Organizations: Caltech, Caltech physics department\n\nFacts:\n- Circa 1979, Chris A. Cole and Stephen Wolfram at Caltech designed the Symbolic Manipulation Program, usually called SMP, as a computer algebra system.\n- Initially, the Caltech physics department developed SMP under Stephen Wolfram's leadership.\n- Geoffrey C. Fox, Jeffrey M. Greif, Eric D. Mjolsness, Larry J. Romans, Timothy Shaw, and Anthony E. Terrano contributed to SMP's initial development.\n- Stephen Wolfram is the author of the book \"A New Kind of Science.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
